        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a277"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts94" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts97">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's it, yeah. We never lack. Even when we're lacking,[laugh] we never lack.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a279"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts102" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts104">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[mhh]</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a280"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts107" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts108">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[inaudible]</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a18"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts109" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts112">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[overlap] Yeah.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a17"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts113" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts114">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah, my biggest fear about us is</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a357"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts117" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts120">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[overlap] because</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a285"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts123" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts125">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Okay</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a19"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts127" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts128">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My Biggest fear about us is.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a20"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts130" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts132">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>that we won't break the cycle.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a287"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts134" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts136">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>because</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a21"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts138" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts140">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As much as I love the love my parents have.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a22"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts142" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts144">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They are very isolated as a consequence of how much they love each other. Do you know what I mean? Like, I remember being very young, and my mum having loads of friends, and my dad having loads of friends, and in my community, everyone is uncle and auntie. Do you know what I mean? But like, they're everywhere. I've got so many friends across the city that are like cousins, but they're just like my mum's brethren's kids and my dad's brethren's kids. But, like,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a23"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts145" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts148">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[laugh] my mum's brethren's kids and my dad's brethren's kids.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a24"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts150" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts152">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Now in their sixties, they don't have that. And I like watched them sacrifice that along the way for the sake of their relationship. A lot of it was for the greater good. And we have had situations where we have had to let friends go because they were actually demonstrating behaviours that were really big red flags. But like,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a25"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts154" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts156">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That really concerns me where</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a26"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts158" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts160">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>For example, when that was your friend, I was really worried about my influence and like my opinions on that person's behaviour and how they were carrying themselves because I didn't want you to make a decision because of how I see things.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a27"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts162" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts164">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If that makes sense, because I have seen my parents do that. I have seen my mum let go of friends because my dad was like, I'm not feeling it. And it's like, I get it. Like, you probably should do that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a28"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts166" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts168">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>But sometimes I just wish for more excitement in their lives that I feel they would have if they had more friends. [overlap] Okay. Whereas now I feel like my mum's life is my dad and his friends.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a29"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts170" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts172">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I don't know. I want more for her. And I want more for me. I want more for us, if that makes sense. So, as much as she is satisfied, I want.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a30"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts174" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts176">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Our relationship to be more than that. I want our relationship to be a foundation of community. Do you know what I mean? I want people to be around. We enjoy hosting, we enjoy having people around, and I.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
